  <p>The supporting chart enums, in full:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>XL_LEGEND_POSITION</code> — <code>TOP</code>, <code>BOTTOM</code>,
      <code>LEFT</code>, <code>RIGHT</code>, <code>CORNER</code>, <code>CUSTOM</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>XL_LABEL_POSITION</code> (also exported as
      <code>XL_DATA_LABEL_POSITION</code>) — <code>ABOVE</code>, <code>BELOW</code>,
      <code>BEST_FIT</code>, <code>CENTER</code>, <code>INSIDE_BASE</code>,
      <code>INSIDE_END</code>, <code>OUTSIDE_END</code>, <code>LEFT</code>, <code>RIGHT</code>,
      <code>MIXED</code>. Which ones a chart accepts depends on its type: bar/column reject
      <code>ABOVE</code>/<code>BELOW</code>, line charts reject <code>INSIDE_END</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>XL_TICK_MARK</code> — <code>NONE</code>, <code>INSIDE</code>,
      <code>OUTSIDE</code>, <code>CROSS</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>XL_TICK_LABEL_POSITION</code> — <code>NONE</code>, <code>LOW</code>,
      <code>HIGH</code>, <code>NEXT_TO_AXIS</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>XL_MARKER_STYLE</code> — <code>AUTOMATIC</code>, <code>NONE</code>,
      <code>CIRCLE</code>, <code>DASH</code>, <code>DIAMOND</code>, <code>DOT</code>,
      <code>PLUS</code>, <code>SQUARE</code>, <code>STAR</code>, <code>TRIANGLE</code>,
      <code>X</code>, <code>PICTURE</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>XL_TRENDLINE_TYPE</code> — <code>LINEAR</code>, <code>POLYNOMIAL</code>,
      <code>EXPONENTIAL</code>, <code>LOGARITHMIC</code>, <code>POWER</code>,
      <code>MOVING_AVERAGE</code>. <code>trendlines.add()</code> also accepts the short names
      <code>"linear"</code>, <code>"poly"</code>, <code>"exp"</code>, <code>"log"</code>,
      <code>"power"</code>, <code>"movingAvg"</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>XL_ERROR_BAR_INCLUDE</code> — <code>FIXED_VALUE</code>, <code>PERCENTAGE</code>,
      <code>STANDARD_DEVIATION</code>, <code>STANDARD_ERROR</code>, <code>CUSTOM</code>;
      <code>XL_ERROR_BAR_TYPE</code> — <code>PLUS</code>, <code>MINUS</code>,
      <code>BOTH</code>; <code>XL_ERROR_BAR_DIRECTION</code> — <code>X</code>, <code>Y</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>XL_AXIS_CROSSES</code> — <code>AUTOMATIC</code>, <code>MINIMUM</code>,
      <code>MAXIMUM</code>, <code>CUSTOM</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>XL_CATEGORY_TYPE</code> — <code>AUTOMATIC_SCALE</code>,
      <code>CATEGORY_SCALE</code>, <code>TIME_SCALE</code>. Reported by
      <code>category_axis.category_type</code>; date categories produce
      <code>TIME_SCALE</code>.
