  <h2 id="other">Actions and languages</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>PP_ACTION</code> (<code>power_pptx.enum.action</code>) — 15 members:
      <code>NONE</code>, <code>HYPERLINK</code>, <code>NAMED_SLIDE</code>,
      <code>NAMED_SLIDE_SHOW</code>, <code>NEXT_SLIDE</code>, <code>PREVIOUS_SLIDE</code>,
      <code>FIRST_SLIDE</code>, <code>LAST_SLIDE</code>, <code>LAST_SLIDE_VIEWED</code>,
      <code>END_SHOW</code>, <code>OPEN_FILE</code>, <code>OLE_VERB</code>, <code>PLAY</code>,
      <code>RUN_MACRO</code>, <code>RUN_PROGRAM</code>. Read off
      <code>shape.click_action.action</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>MSO_LANGUAGE_ID</code> (<code>power_pptx.enum.lang</code>) — 214 locale ids, assigned
      to <code>font.language_id</code> to steer PowerPoint's spell-checker.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="gotchas">Gotchas</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>MSO_PATTERN_TYPE.ERCENT_40</code> is the upstream typo (missing leading "P"). It is
      kept as an alias for compatibility and raises <code>DeprecationWarning</code> on access —
      use <code>PERCENT_40</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Many enums ship under two names. The aliases are the <em>same object</em>, so
      <code>MSO_ANCHOR.MIDDLE is MSO_VERTICAL_ANCHOR.MIDDLE</code> is <code>True</code> — pick one
      spelling per codebase and stay with it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>MIXED</code> members exist only for parity with the Microsoft object model, where they
      report "the selection has more than one value". They have no XML representation, so never
      assign one; treat them as read-only sentinels.
    </li>
    <li>
      Members are <code>int</code>-valued, so <code>PP_ALIGN.CENTER == 2</code> is
      <code>True</code>. Don't lean on that — write the member name, which survives an upstream
      renumbering.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>add_shape</code> and <code>add_chart</code> do <strong>not</strong> accept short-name
      strings; a lower-case <code>"rounded_rectangle"</code> raises <code>KeyError</code>. Pass the
      enum member.
    </li>
  </ul>

